INT. DRY DOCK PUMP ROOM - NIGHT

Concrete. Sweating pipes. A single caged bulb.

KOVAC (50s, heavy coat, never takes his hands from his pockets) sits on an upturned crate.

IRINA VESK (40s, wet hair, steady eyes) stands by the door. Doesn't sit.

KOVAC
You're late.

IRINA
Traffic.

KOVAC
There's no traffic at this hour.

IRINA
Then I took the long way.

KOVAC
Why?

IRINA
Habit.

KOVAC
Whose habit? Yours or his?

IRINA
Whose do you think?

KOVAC
I think you're still counting the exits.

IRINA
Two. The door and the one behind you.

KOVAC
Three. You forgot the grate.

IRINA
I didn't forget it.

KOVAC
Good. Then you know why I picked this room.

IRINA
Because the water's loud.

KOVAC
Because the water's loud. Nobody hears anything down here.

IRINA
Nobody's supposed to.

KOVAC
You brought it?

IRINA
You brought the other half?

KOVAC
I asked first.

IRINA
And I'm still standing.

KOVAC
That's not an answer.

IRINA
It's the only one you get until I see yours.

KOVAC
Fair.

IRINA
Show me.

KOVAC
Slowly, then.

IRINA
Slowly.

KOVAC
You first. Left hand.

IRINA
Right hand. Always the right.

KOVAC
You're not in charge here.

IRINA
Neither are you.

Somewhere above, a pump shudders on. Neither of them blinks.
